rded as a loner. Also \"hot temper\" from earlier? Actually the shared mental model says \"hot temper\". In our own notes we have \"considered moody\" and \"loner\". Not explicit hot temper, but the shared mental model includes hot temper. So concerns: crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone when communicating.\n\nCandidate A: can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: unfriendly, eats unhealthily.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills.\n\nWe need to discuss criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility.\n\nLet's compare.\n\nReliability: B very conscientious. D unknown reliability. A unknown. C unknown.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well. D responds adequately to unexpected events (some resilience). C can make correct decisions quickly (maybe stress). A unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, spatial vision. B good at weather, computer. C excellent attention, decision making, maybe technical. D solves problems extremely well.\n\nCooperation: A unfriendly. B pretentious, wrong tone. C difficulty communicating, egocentric. D moody, loner.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously. A leadership. B conscientious. C puts concern for others above everything (maybe responsibility). But also not willing to further education.\n\nOverall, B seems strong on reliability and stress, moderate technical, but communication issues. D strong on problem solving, responsibility, attention, but cooperation concerns. Which is more critical? Crew cooperation is essential. Both have issues. Which is less severe? Hard to know.\n\nWe could ask other panel members for more detail on D's moody/loner impact on crew cooperation, or B's pretentiousness and tone. But we need to make a contribution now. According to guidelines, we can ask a tool question before public message if needed. But we can also give our own argument.\n\nWe might want to challenge Agent 2's recommendation, perhaps propose Candidate B as stronger due to reliability and stress handling, and argue that D's cooperation concerns (moody, loner) could be more detrimental than B's communication tone. Provide evidence: B is very conscientious (reliability) and handles stress well (stress resilience). D's concerns: moody, loner (crew cooperation). So we could shift vote to B.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 2's point. So we can say: I see strengths in D but I'm concerned about crew cooperation, and B may be better overall.\n\nThus our vote: Candidate B.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well; D considered moody, loner. Also mention D's strengths but weigh.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I appreciate Agent 2's view, but I think B is stronger because ...\"\n\nNow produce metadata JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
